Third-party components and their licenses
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. YOLOv5 (Ultralytics) — AGPL-3.0
   https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5

   `septo_sympto.py` loads YOLOv5 at runtime via `torch.hub.load()`. YOLOv5 is
   NOT vendored in this repository; it is downloaded from GitHub at the pinned
   tag v7.0 on first run.

   IMPORTANT — pre-trained weights:
   The pycnidia detection weights (`pycnidia-model.pt`) were produced by
   training with Ultralytics YOLOv5. Ultralytics takes the position that models
   trained with their software are derivative works and inherit the AGPL-3.0
   license. Accordingly, `pycnidia-model.pt` is distributed under AGPL-3.0, not
   under the MIT License that covers this repository's source code.

   Practical consequence: if you deploy SeptoSympto as a network service using
   these pycnidia weights, AGPL-3.0 obligations may apply to that deployment.
   Retraining the pycnidia detector with a non-AGPL architecture would remove
   this constraint. This is a stated goal of the ongoing rework.

2. U-Net necrosis weights (`necrosis-model-375.h5`)
   Trained with the authors' own U-Net implementation
   (https://github.com/maximereder/unet) on TensorFlow/Keras, which is
   Apache-2.0. No copyleft obligation attaches to these weights; they are
   covered by this repository's MIT License.

3. TensorFlow (Apache-2.0), PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause), OpenCV (Apache-2.0),
   NumPy / pandas / SciPy (BSD-3-Clause).
   These are ordinary runtime dependencies installed from PyPI and are not
   redistributed by this repository.

